WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.425
Lesson 13.2.

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:06.080
Risk-adjusted yield: subtracting expected losses.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.200
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.779
able to convert every headline yield into an

00:00:10.779 --> 00:00:14.045
expected yield after the losses it statistically carries.

00:00:15.345 --> 00:00:16.635
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:18.320
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.035
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:22.560
Then, your checklist.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.722
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:26.022 --> 00:00:30.312
risk-adjusted yield = headline − (annual loss probability

00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:33.270
× loss given default) − costs You don't

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.672
know the true loss probability, so write down

00:00:36.672 --> 00:00:39.487
an assumption and be conservative.

00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:41.842
Newer protocols, more dependencies and

00:00:41.842 --> 00:00:44.497
higher leverage deserve higher numbers.

00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:47.029
The point isn't precision; it's making you

00:00:47.029 --> 00:00:49.267
compare positions on the same footing.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.914
the calculator The 9% vault still wins on

00:00:53.914 --> 00:00:57.242
expectation, but by 2 points, not 4.5.

00:00:57.242 --> 00:00:59.949
Its bad outcome is also far worse,

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:02.802
so size it smaller (Lesson 13.3).

00:01:02.802 --> 00:01:10.112
New protocol vault, 9.0%, 3%/yr, 100%, 6.0%.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:17.552
Blue-chip lending, 4.5%, 0.5%/yr, 100%, 4.0%.

00:01:18.852 --> 00:01:20.312
Here's your checklist.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:21.847
Do it now, for real.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:26.042
First, Loss probability and LGD written for every position.

00:01:26.042 --> 00:01:29.872
And finally, Decisions made on risk-adjusted, not headline.

00:01:31.172 --> 00:01:32.382
Question 1.

00:01:32.382 --> 00:01:38.112
12% headline, 5%/yr loss probability, 60% LGD.

00:01:38.112 --> 00:01:39.157
Risk-adjusted?

00:01:43.577 --> 00:01:46.713
The answer: 12 − 3 = 9%.

00:01:48.013 --> 00:01:49.258
Question 2.

00:01:49.258 --> 00:01:50.873
Why assume conservatively?

00:01:55.293 --> 00:01:58.453
The answer: Losses cluster in stress, when many

00:01:58.453 --> 00:02:02.733
positions fail together; optimistic assumptions overstate income.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.303
Question 3.

00:02:05.303 --> 00:02:08.173
Two positions, same risk-adjusted yield.

00:02:08.173 --> 00:02:09.488
Which gets more capital?

00:02:13.908 --> 00:02:15.462
The answer: The one with the

00:02:15.462 --> 00:02:17.658
smaller and better-understood worst case.

00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:21.473
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:25.573
Next up, Lesson 13.3: Building the income portfolio.
